<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leopold II, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1747">1747</a>–<a href="/years/1792">1792</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Pietro Leopoldo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leopold II, known in Tuscany as Peter Leopold, was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i-holy-roman-emperor">Francis Stephen of Lorraine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> who ruled the Grand Duchy of Tuscany from 1765 to 1790. An enlightened reformer, he freed the grain trade, reorganised the administration and in 1786 made Tuscany the first state to abolish torture and the death penalty. In 1790 he succeeded his brother Joseph II as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leopold-ii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Leopold II, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anton Hickel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anton_Hickel_-_Portrait_of_Emperor_Leopold_II,_formerly_identified_as_Joseph_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
